WEBVTT


00:00:26.720 --> 00:00:29.550
<i>Like all things on this hurtling sphere...</i>


00:00:29.720 --> 00:00:33.380
<i>...I emerged from the molten center
of creation.</i>


00:00:34.670 --> 00:00:37.420
<i>But mine has been a unique path.</i>


00:00:37.590 --> 00:00:42.930
<i>Isolated, I developed attributes
beyond those of lesser beings.</i>


00:00:46.590 --> 00:00:50.630
<i>Then the sphere was struck
by a vast celestial stone.</i>


00:00:53.340 --> 00:00:57.050
<i>Black chunks of death filled the skies...</i>


00:00:57.220 --> 00:01:00.930
<i>...and the world
became a chaotic garden of doom.</i>


00:01:02.300 --> 00:01:06.260
<i>Soon the sphere began
to nurture new kinds of life.</i>


00:01:06.420 --> 00:01:09.140
<i>And there was one
that stood above all the rest.</i>


00:01:09.300 --> 00:01:12.420
<i>Its fragile shell belied its vicious nature.</i>


00:01:12.590 --> 00:01:14.510
<i>And in what seemed like a heartbeat...</i>


00:01:14.760 --> 00:01:20.010
<i>...these things proliferated in both number
and destructive means.</i>


00:01:22.590 --> 00:01:26.420
<i>Now they have harnessed
the most destructive force.</i>


00:01:27.930 --> 00:01:31.930
<i>And I, The Centre, have concluded...</i>


00:01:32.090 --> 00:01:35.720
<i>...that the sphere
must be cleansed of them.</i>


00:04:02.220 --> 00:04:04.970
<i>This is Lois Lane on Armed Forces Radio.</i>


00:04:05.140 --> 00:04:08.970
<i>Well, boys, it looks like the party's over.
They signed the ceasefire.</i>


00:04:09.140 --> 00:04:11.590
<i>So have a drink and smoke them
if you got them.</i>


00:04:11.930 --> 00:04:14.140
<i>We're going home.</i>


00:04:20.510 --> 00:04:24.140
Some way to end a war, huh, kid?
Nobody wins, nobody loses.


00:04:24.300 --> 00:04:26.800
Long as it's over, Ace. I got plans.


00:04:26.970 --> 00:04:29.460
Right, I forgot.
You're gonna be a space ranger.


00:04:30.800 --> 00:04:33.220
The proper term is "test pilot,"
funny man.


00:04:33.590 --> 00:04:36.970
I'm gonna see the stars, close up.


00:04:38.420 --> 00:04:39.880
Hey.


00:04:43.380 --> 00:04:45.970
Sons of bitches must not have heard
about the ceasefire.


00:04:49.590 --> 00:04:53.340
<i>I'm coming back for you.
Try using your guns for a change.</i>


00:05:06.460 --> 00:05:07.970
<i>Can you make it back now, Ace?</i>


00:05:08.180 --> 00:05:10.760
Roger that.
Gotta get me a new pair of skivvies.


00:05:12.420 --> 00:05:14.260
Got another bogey.


00:05:19.550 --> 00:05:21.670
<i>Hal, your engine.</i>


00:05:21.840 --> 00:05:23.180
<i>Punch out. Punch out!</i>


00:06:08.180 --> 00:06:11.300
Listen to me. War over.


00:06:12.630 --> 00:06:14.050
Finished.


00:06:33.140 --> 00:06:34.760
It's over.


00:06:35.340 --> 00:06:38.010
War over.


00:07:01.670 --> 00:07:03.930
I'm so sorry.


00:07:04.090 --> 00:07:09.090
All I wanted was to send a signal
to Mars.


00:07:09.930 --> 00:07:13.970
How could I have known
it would teleport you here?


00:07:17.460 --> 00:07:20.970
I suppose we both got the shock
of our lives.


00:07:22.140 --> 00:07:26.930
But your heart must be stronger
than mine.


00:07:27.300 --> 00:07:29.880
Whoever you are...


00:07:31.300 --> 00:07:33.970
...forgive me.


00:08:29.510 --> 00:08:30.670
Come on in, Kal.


00:08:31.380 --> 00:08:33.180
Join the celebration.


00:08:33.630 --> 00:08:35.880
Diana, what's going on here?


00:08:36.460 --> 00:08:38.460
Tell them they'd be wasting their bullets.


00:08:40.260 --> 00:08:43.800
Don't judge them, KaI.
They get a little nervous around men now.


00:08:44.050 --> 00:08:46.550
What are you talking about?
-I was heading upriver...


00:08:46.720 --> 00:08:49.050
...when I passed this village
about four days ago.


00:08:49.220 --> 00:08:52.050
The people here helped the French.
The rebels didn't like that.


00:08:52.220 --> 00:08:55.380
They murdered the men and children
and they threw them in the river.


00:08:55.550 --> 00:09:01.010
<i>These women were beaten and penned
in tiger cages for the rebels to use.</i>


00:09:02.050 --> 00:09:04.300
<i>The rebels, how did they die?</i>


00:09:04.460 --> 00:09:05.970
<i>I only disarmed them.</i>


00:09:08.300 --> 00:09:11.880
<i>I left their guns in a clearing and
then I let the women out of their cages.</i>


00:09:17.460 --> 00:09:19.140
They did this?


00:09:19.300 --> 00:09:21.340
And you just stood by and watched?


00:09:21.510 --> 00:09:23.760
I gave them freedom
and a chance for justice.


00:09:23.930 --> 00:09:27.140
You know, the American way.


00:09:27.510 --> 00:09:30.140
This is what the government's afraid of,
Diana.


00:09:30.300 --> 00:09:32.380
Us acting like vigilantes.


00:09:32.550 --> 00:09:34.550
I have to do what I think is right.


00:09:34.970 --> 00:09:37.220
That's what the others said at first,
remember?


00:09:37.510 --> 00:09:40.760
And now Batman's a fugitive,
the whole Justice Society's retired...


00:09:40.930 --> 00:09:42.880
...and Hourman's dead.


00:09:43.380 --> 00:09:44.840
No matter how much good we do...


00:09:45.010 --> 00:09:48.050
...deep down, people are always
going to be scared of us.


00:09:48.380 --> 00:09:51.220
Isn't that why you and I
signed those loyalty oaths?


00:09:51.380 --> 00:09:52.720
Take a look around, Kal.


00:09:53.340 --> 00:09:55.340
Oaths don't mean much here.


00:09:55.510 --> 00:09:57.760
All I see is suffering and madness.


00:09:58.760 --> 00:10:01.460
But...
-There's the door, spaceman.


00:10:03.300 --> 00:10:04.760
Yeah.


00:10:04.930 --> 00:10:06.800
Yeah, yeah, yeah.


00:10:06.970 --> 00:10:08.510
Yeah.


00:10:51.140 --> 00:10:55.630
<i>The downed pilot insisted
the island was teeming with dinosaurs...</i>


00:10:55.800 --> 00:10:58.180
<i>...but Navy sources claim
a search revealed...</i>


00:10:58.340 --> 00:11:03.090
<i>...that not only were there no dinosaurs,
there wasn't even an island.</i>


00:11:03.260 --> 00:11:04.630
<i>In other news-</i>


00:11:04.800 --> 00:11:08.010
<i>Well, I don't know, Groucho,
that's not really what I meant.</i>


00:11:08.180 --> 00:11:11.510
<i>We keep our farm animals in the farm,
not in the house.</i>


00:11:11.670 --> 00:11:13.970
<i>Not in the bedroom, certainly.</i>


00:11:16.050 --> 00:11:18.800
<i>Eh, what's up, doc?</i>


00:11:22.090 --> 00:11:25.180
<i>This now concludes our broadcasting day.</i>


00:11:32.930 --> 00:11:35.550
The last I heard,
she went back to Paradise Island.


00:11:35.720 --> 00:11:37.590
It sounds like she's lost her mind.


00:11:38.840 --> 00:11:40.550
I don't think it's that simple.


00:11:40.720 --> 00:11:43.050
Diana's an Amazon
who's become an American.


00:11:43.220 --> 00:11:45.550
She's trying to make sense
of her convictions.


00:11:45.720 --> 00:11:48.670
Between her and that Batman character...


00:11:48.840 --> 00:11:51.720
I thought these people were your friends.
-They are.


00:11:51.880 --> 00:11:54.970
But neither of them would sacrifice
their principles for a friend.


00:11:55.140 --> 00:11:58.380
Ever since McCarthy came to-
-McCarthy. He's no excuse.


00:11:58.550 --> 00:12:02.880
Whatever party, whatever administration,
there'll always be boogeymen like him.


00:12:03.050 --> 00:12:04.840
We need our heroes to stand up...


00:12:04.970 --> 00:12:08.340
...and show us what this country
is supposed to mean.


00:12:11.420 --> 00:12:14.050
We need a leader.


00:12:31.930 --> 00:12:34.220
Come on, rolI it.
Come on, eight. Come on, eight.


00:12:34.380 --> 00:12:35.880
Yes.


00:12:37.840 --> 00:12:39.670
Ten's the number to win.


00:12:39.840 --> 00:12:42.340
Now why don't you tell me
what we're doing here, Ace?


00:12:42.510 --> 00:12:45.090
Told you, HaI, it's a surprise.


00:12:45.510 --> 00:12:46.800
You'll find out tomorrow.


00:12:47.260 --> 00:12:50.380
Now, roll those dice before they cool off.


00:12:54.340 --> 00:12:55.720
Come on, 10.


00:12:56.180 --> 00:12:58.180
Ten. It's a winner.


00:13:00.420 --> 00:13:02.880
And you have the loveliest light
in your eyes, dig?


00:13:03.050 --> 00:13:07.630
Can we get back to the interview, please?
-Oh, yeah. My philosophy of life.


00:13:07.800 --> 00:13:11.050
Tell your readers they gotta do what I do,
live for the moment...


00:13:11.220 --> 00:13:14.220
...because it might be our last,
you dig, Miss West?


00:13:14.380 --> 00:13:16.550
Very profound.
-That's me.


00:13:16.720 --> 00:13:20.970
I've always been, you know,
deep like that.


00:13:22.090 --> 00:13:23.550
Time for the sound check, boss.


00:13:27.720 --> 00:13:29.930
Back in a moment.


00:13:30.300 --> 00:13:32.460
I'll try to live for it.


00:13:34.010 --> 00:13:37.840
<i>I tell you, these two heavyweights
are giving us quite a show tonight.</i>


00:13:38.760 --> 00:13:41.380
<i>Oh, it looks like it'Il have to wait
for the next round, folks.</i>


00:13:41.550 --> 00:13:43.090
<i>Meantime, we've got the champ...</i>


00:13:44.420 --> 00:13:46.550
<i>...Ted "Wildcat" Grant,
solidly ahead on points.</i>


00:13:46.720 --> 00:13:48.180
<i>Uh, hello.
-Hello, Barry?</i>


00:13:48.340 --> 00:13:50.590
Iris. I thought you had to work tonight.


00:13:50.970 --> 00:13:52.010
I do.


00:13:52.180 --> 00:13:54.630
But I wanted to tell you
how much I miss you.


00:13:54.800 --> 00:13:57.460
You have no idea.
-Come on, how could you miss me?


00:13:57.630 --> 00:14:00.760
You're in Las Vegas interviewing
all those singers and movie stars.


00:14:00.930 --> 00:14:01.970
<i>It's the fast lane.</i>


00:14:02.140 --> 00:14:05.590
There are lots of potholes
in that lane, let me tell you.


00:14:07.670 --> 00:14:09.180
Iris? Iris.


00:14:15.550 --> 00:14:19.720
Sorry to interrupt your festivities,
but if you all stay calm...


00:14:19.880 --> 00:14:25.010
...we'll be gone as soon as my friends here
come back from the cashiers' booths.


00:14:29.340 --> 00:14:33.380
The key phrase was "stay calm. "


00:14:36.670 --> 00:14:37.970
<i>Iris, what's happening?</i>


00:14:38.300 --> 00:14:39.670
You there.


00:14:40.050 --> 00:14:42.720
The naughty girl on the phone.


00:14:44.880 --> 00:14:46.140
Iris!


00:15:04.630 --> 00:15:06.760
Just a few more seconds, everyone.


00:15:08.380 --> 00:15:10.090
Ah, my ride is here.


00:15:25.260 --> 00:15:27.260
Wait.


00:15:28.300 --> 00:15:29.340
Make it quick.


00:15:30.380 --> 00:15:33.340
Hot damn, Ace.
It's that super-fast guy from CentraI City.


00:15:33.550 --> 00:15:35.590
The Flash. He'll take care of this clown.


00:15:35.970 --> 00:15:38.140
I took precautions
in case you dropped by.


00:15:38.510 --> 00:15:39.930
If you so much as touch me...


00:15:40.090 --> 00:15:43.420
...you'Il trigger six cryogenic bombs
I've hidden around the city.


00:15:43.590 --> 00:15:47.140
And they'll go off in 90 seconds anyway,
unless you find them.


00:15:47.510 --> 00:15:53.460
So it's your choice now.
Me, or the city and everyone in it.


00:15:53.630 --> 00:15:55.800
Eighty-nine, 88-


00:16:00.010 --> 00:16:01.050
One...


00:16:01.630 --> 00:16:02.930
...two, three, four...


00:16:05.800 --> 00:16:08.930
...five. Where's six?


00:16:53.840 --> 00:16:56.720
It took me a second or two,
but I figured out the sixth bomb...


00:16:56.930 --> 00:16:58.670
...was just a wild-goose chase.


00:16:58.840 --> 00:17:03.720
You are different
from the other lesser beings. Faster.


00:17:03.880 --> 00:17:06.880
Why?
-Lesser beings?


00:17:07.050 --> 00:17:08.380
What are you talking about?


00:17:11.050 --> 00:17:12.720
Eh? Wha-?


00:17:15.630 --> 00:17:16.670
What did you do?


00:17:16.840 --> 00:17:19.180
I rewired it on the way down.


00:17:27.550 --> 00:17:30.510
Don't ever mess with my Iris.


00:18:10.090 --> 00:18:11.460
This little trip's been fun.


00:18:11.630 --> 00:18:13.840
Are you ever gonna tell me
where we're headed?


00:18:14.010 --> 00:18:17.090
To hell if you don't slow down.
What's wrong with you?


00:18:17.260 --> 00:18:19.760
Ever since you got out of the hospitaI...


00:18:19.930 --> 00:18:21.800
It was Korea.


00:18:22.670 --> 00:18:23.930
Changed everything.


00:18:24.300 --> 00:18:26.090
Wars have a tendency to do that.


00:18:26.260 --> 00:18:28.800
Look, Ace, you know
that ever since I was a kid...


00:18:28.970 --> 00:18:32.550
...watching my old man fly,
I wanted to see the stars.


00:18:32.720 --> 00:18:34.880
But the war and then the hospital...


00:18:35.340 --> 00:18:37.380
...it's like I'm damaged goods.


00:18:37.550 --> 00:18:41.300
I can't get a first-class outfit
to take me on. And without a ride...


00:18:41.840 --> 00:18:43.460
...I sure can't climb the pyramid.


00:18:44.380 --> 00:18:46.460
Slow down.
-Why bother?


00:18:46.840 --> 00:18:49.670
You have to, kid, because we're here.


00:19:03.420 --> 00:19:06.180
It's where you get your second chance.


00:19:07.510 --> 00:19:09.670
<i>How did you know he was the commie?</i>


00:19:09.840 --> 00:19:13.010
<i>He came back for the formula,
that's what nailed it.</i>


00:19:13.420 --> 00:19:14.880
<i>He could've killed you.</i>


00:19:15.050 --> 00:19:17.670
<i>Like I always say,
when you know you're right...</i>


00:19:18.090 --> 00:19:19.670
<i>...it's worth taking a chance.</i>


00:19:20.140 --> 00:19:22.180
<i>Now, come here.</i>


00:19:42.300 --> 00:19:45.880
Ace Morgan's recommendation
carries a lot of weight at Ferris Aircraft.


00:19:46.220 --> 00:19:48.220
I assume he spoke as well of us to you.


00:19:48.510 --> 00:19:53.050
He did. And I can't imagine anywhere else
I'd rather be right now, Miss Ferris.


00:19:54.010 --> 00:19:56.550
Do you have any questions?


00:19:57.220 --> 00:19:59.720
I'm surprised your father
isn't interviewing me.


00:19:59.880 --> 00:20:02.720
Not that I mind, it's just that you're a-
-A woman?


00:20:02.880 --> 00:20:05.880
My father trusts me with the day-to-day
operation of the company.


00:20:06.050 --> 00:20:09.090
If that's good enough for him, it ought to-
-Whoa, wait.


00:20:09.260 --> 00:20:13.840
I was only saying that you're a little young
to be running a major corporation.


00:20:14.260 --> 00:20:16.590
Oh. Oh, you're good, flyboy...


00:20:16.760 --> 00:20:19.090
...but save it for the girls
in the typing pool.


00:20:19.260 --> 00:20:20.590
One last question.


00:20:20.760 --> 00:20:24.380
In your resume, there's a gap
between July and December of '53.


00:20:25.180 --> 00:20:27.380
I was in a VA hospitaI.


00:20:27.550 --> 00:20:28.590
Psych ward.


00:20:31.050 --> 00:20:33.590
Most people wouldn't talk about
this kind of thing...


00:20:33.760 --> 00:20:35.720
...but I learned a lot about myself there.


00:20:35.880 --> 00:20:38.930
I came out knowing who I really am
and what I really want.


00:20:40.340 --> 00:20:43.380
You report for training
and security clearance in two weeks.


00:20:44.090 --> 00:20:45.670
All right, let's celebrate.


00:20:45.840 --> 00:20:48.010
Waiter, some champagne.


00:20:48.180 --> 00:20:51.510
Look, HaI,
I don't get involved with my employees.


00:20:51.670 --> 00:20:52.760
I understand, Carol...


00:20:53.140 --> 00:20:55.220
...but I don't start work
for two more weeks.


00:20:56.760 --> 00:20:58.180
Two glasses.


00:21:02.720 --> 00:21:06.670
So where'd this hot tip come from, John?
-A source.


00:21:07.930 --> 00:21:09.800
WelI, I think I know your secret.


00:21:10.460 --> 00:21:12.050
You do?
-Hm.


00:21:12.300 --> 00:21:14.220
The tips you get from out of the blue...


00:21:14.380 --> 00:21:17.220
...those hunches of yours
that always turn out to be right.


00:21:18.510 --> 00:21:20.260
You're dating a fortuneteller.


00:21:20.630 --> 00:21:22.090
No, I-


00:21:23.880 --> 00:21:25.800
Something like that.


00:21:35.420 --> 00:21:38.760
Try the back.
I'll see if I can pick this lock.


00:22:25.670 --> 00:22:27.090
You are the tribute.


00:22:27.260 --> 00:22:29.930
Yours is the glory
of nourishing the strength...


00:22:30.180 --> 00:22:32.260
...of The Centre.


00:22:44.090 --> 00:22:46.010
You okay, John?


00:22:55.590 --> 00:22:57.420
No, stay away.


00:22:57.590 --> 00:22:59.380
Stay away!


00:22:59.550 --> 00:23:02.260
Back off, you're scaring the boy.


00:23:04.720 --> 00:23:06.840
You'll be alI right now that-


00:23:13.010 --> 00:23:14.930
You wilI be judged too.


00:23:15.970 --> 00:23:18.140
You wilI all be judged.


00:23:18.300 --> 00:23:22.180
Without The Centre, there is no holding.


00:23:22.840 --> 00:23:26.010
The Centre? What's The Centre?


00:23:51.340 --> 00:23:52.840
<i>Jordan, do you copy?</i>


00:23:53.140 --> 00:23:55.840
<i>Negative, Colonel Flagg, no Jordan here...</i>


00:23:56.630 --> 00:23:58.970
<i>-... just Spam in a can.
Cut the comedy.</i>


00:23:59.300 --> 00:24:01.630
Are you go for 72?


00:24:01.800 --> 00:24:03.840
<i>Yes, Captain Personality.</i>


00:24:04.010 --> 00:24:06.460
<i>Jordan is go for exercise 72.</i>


00:24:06.930 --> 00:24:09.800
<i>Hit it.
-My pleasure.</i>


00:24:30.420 --> 00:24:34.340
Spam Jordan is now go for exercise 73.


00:24:35.300 --> 00:24:37.970
How's he doing?
-He's tough enough, that's for sure.


00:24:38.140 --> 00:24:41.260
But I'm getting sick of his attitude.
-He's a pilot, ColoneI Flagg.


00:24:41.420 --> 00:24:43.800
He's used to making decisions
and being in control.


00:24:43.970 --> 00:24:45.970
This training goes against his nature.


00:24:46.220 --> 00:24:48.510
Can't be helped.
It's all part of the big picture.


00:24:48.840 --> 00:24:51.180
Which he hasn't seen yet.


00:24:57.460 --> 00:24:58.630
CaroI.


00:24:59.050 --> 00:25:01.010
I mean, Miss Ferris, afternoon.


00:25:01.180 --> 00:25:04.420
Afternoon, Mr. Jordan.
I trust ColoneI Flagg is keeping you busy.


00:25:04.590 --> 00:25:07.380
This stuff? Child's play, Miss Ferris.


00:25:07.550 --> 00:25:09.510
Perhaps later I could show you-
Jordan.


00:25:09.670 --> 00:25:12.090
What?
-Exercise 73, remember?


00:25:12.260 --> 00:25:14.880
Yeah, they tell me 73's the charm.


00:25:15.050 --> 00:25:17.050
Good day, Miss Ferris.


00:25:22.010 --> 00:25:23.880
What are his numbers, Harry?
-Uh...


00:25:24.050 --> 00:25:27.010
Excellent.
Responses in the 99th percentile.


00:25:29.340 --> 00:25:30.010
Hm.


00:25:43.050 --> 00:25:46.340
Not that I'm complaining,
but where exactly are you taking me?


00:25:46.760 --> 00:25:50.220
Where have you always wanted to go?
-That's a leading question.


00:25:50.380 --> 00:25:52.220
No, I mean, since you were a kid.


00:25:52.380 --> 00:25:55.510
Your big goal?
-The stars.


00:25:55.670 --> 00:25:59.670
But at the rate we're going, the Russians
are gonna beat us into orbit by months.


00:25:59.840 --> 00:26:02.300
Who said anything about orbit?


00:26:02.460 --> 00:26:04.180
Whoa!


00:26:20.670 --> 00:26:21.840
A hole in the ground.


00:26:22.260 --> 00:26:23.840
Isn't that the wrong direction?


00:26:24.180 --> 00:26:27.220
Sometimes you have to go through hell
to get to heaven.


00:26:36.590 --> 00:26:38.760
What is all this?


00:26:41.180 --> 00:26:43.760
Welcome to the reaI Ferris Aircraft.


00:27:00.630 --> 00:27:02.420
See that sour-looking man down there?


00:27:02.720 --> 00:27:03.880
He'Il explain everything.


00:27:04.880 --> 00:27:06.260
His name's Faraday.


00:27:06.420 --> 00:27:08.630
Works for the government.


00:27:08.970 --> 00:27:11.880
And if you like Rick Flagg,
you'll love him.


00:27:13.630 --> 00:27:16.050
You're weak, erratic, emotional...


00:27:16.220 --> 00:27:20.460
...and for my money, at least a little pink.
But I'm told you're the best we've got.


00:27:21.970 --> 00:27:23.590
I...
-You keep your mouth shut...


00:27:23.930 --> 00:27:25.050
...and your ears open.


00:27:25.220 --> 00:27:28.510
I'm about to share some of this nation's
greatest secrets with you.


00:27:37.590 --> 00:27:41.800
Couple of years ago, we found the body
of a radical scientist named Erdel...


00:27:41.970 --> 00:27:44.180
...in a small observatory near Gotham.


00:27:44.340 --> 00:27:47.140
Somehow,
he'd been able to contact Mars.


00:27:47.840 --> 00:27:50.460
Mars? You're joking, right?


00:27:50.760 --> 00:27:54.050
Yes, Jordan, I'm a real kidder.


00:27:54.720 --> 00:27:57.510
We found this footprint
at the observatory.


00:27:58.930 --> 00:28:01.340
Did you find what made that print?


00:28:01.510 --> 00:28:02.590
No.


00:28:03.050 --> 00:28:06.630
Whatever it is,
it's eluded us for two years.


00:28:07.050 --> 00:28:09.090
There's life on Mars, Jordan.


00:28:09.260 --> 00:28:10.970
And it's come to Earth.


00:28:12.010 --> 00:28:14.970
Look, I'm just a pilot.
What does this have to do with me?


00:28:23.380 --> 00:28:25.300
You haven't figured it out yet?


00:28:25.970 --> 00:28:28.380
We've got to know what these Martians
want from us...


00:28:28.550 --> 00:28:31.220
...and since we can't find them
here on Earth...


00:28:31.720 --> 00:28:33.140
...we're going to Mars.


00:28:37.630 --> 00:28:39.550
Outstanding.


00:28:48.420 --> 00:28:50.590
Welcome home, Mr. Jones.


00:28:50.760 --> 00:28:51.760
Why didn't I-?


00:28:51.930 --> 00:28:53.930
Why didn't you sense me as you do others?


00:28:55.300 --> 00:28:56.340
That's my secret.


00:28:57.140 --> 00:28:59.840
Why are you here?
Because of The Centre?


00:29:00.180 --> 00:29:03.460
The cult's spreading all over the world.


00:29:03.630 --> 00:29:05.840
At first I thought it might be
the communists.


00:29:06.010 --> 00:29:08.140
But they're having trouble
with the cults too.


00:29:08.300 --> 00:29:09.670
It's not ideologicaI.


00:29:09.970 --> 00:29:11.970
There's some kind
of psychic force involved.


00:29:12.140 --> 00:29:14.590
It's affecting people
with high susceptibility.


00:29:15.050 --> 00:29:17.220
Getting into their minds.


00:29:17.380 --> 00:29:18.590
I felt it.


00:29:18.930 --> 00:29:22.090
Yes, your feelings. How-?


00:29:22.260 --> 00:29:24.420
Let's just say that's my secret.


00:29:24.590 --> 00:29:27.420
You came here because
you want to work together, true?


00:29:27.590 --> 00:29:30.140
True.
-Then we'll share our information.


00:29:31.140 --> 00:29:32.800
I've already collected some.


00:29:37.630 --> 00:29:38.930
Newspaper clippings.


00:29:39.090 --> 00:29:41.260
You'll have to do better than that.


00:29:41.760 --> 00:29:46.800
And one other thing, I'm not sure
what you are or where you come from...


00:29:46.970 --> 00:29:50.050
...but my instincts tell me
you're to be trusted.


00:29:50.220 --> 00:29:52.050
Make no mistake, though.


00:29:52.220 --> 00:29:54.840
I have a $70,000 sliver
of radioactive meteor...


00:29:55.010 --> 00:29:56.630
...to stop the one from Metropolis.


00:29:56.970 --> 00:30:01.010
With you, all I need is a penny
for a book of matches.


00:30:19.460 --> 00:30:22.760
What's the matter, Grodd,
feeling starved for attention?


00:30:50.090 --> 00:30:52.220
You're government property now, swifty.


00:30:52.380 --> 00:30:55.180
We're gonna find out
what makes you tick.


00:31:03.300 --> 00:31:04.720
Hey.
Did you see that?


00:31:04.880 --> 00:31:06.760
Where did he go?


00:31:15.220 --> 00:31:17.380
What you got there, John?


00:31:18.300 --> 00:31:20.010
A kids' book?
-Not exactly.


00:31:20.180 --> 00:31:22.590
The author committed suicide
a while back.


00:31:22.760 --> 00:31:24.760
He thought the world was about to end.


00:31:24.930 --> 00:31:26.840
You like this weird stuff, don't you?


00:31:27.010 --> 00:31:30.300
WelI, you should see what they got
in the interrogation room.


00:31:31.300 --> 00:31:33.260
He shot a cop on the parkway.


00:31:33.420 --> 00:31:35.090
Then we found his mother...


00:31:35.260 --> 00:31:37.090
...in his trunk.


00:31:37.460 --> 00:31:39.550
Mental case?
-Not your typical one.


00:31:39.720 --> 00:31:42.180
This guy's a scientist.


00:31:44.930 --> 00:31:48.010
You're here to kill me, aren't you?
You're part of it.


00:31:48.180 --> 00:31:50.260
I'm not going to kill you.


00:31:50.420 --> 00:31:52.510
And what do you think I'm part of?


00:31:52.670 --> 00:31:54.760
The Centre. It's everywhere.


00:31:55.590 --> 00:31:57.220
What do you know about The Centre?


00:31:57.380 --> 00:32:00.260
It's gonna kill everyone.
I was trying to get away from it.


00:32:00.420 --> 00:32:02.050
How do you know alI this?


00:32:02.420 --> 00:32:05.840
I just do. I can feel it.


00:32:06.260 --> 00:32:10.260
I tried to get in on the Mars mission
but they wouldn't take me.


00:32:10.420 --> 00:32:11.840
The Mars mission?


00:32:12.180 --> 00:32:14.720
Yes. They're going to Mars.
It's safe there.


00:32:14.880 --> 00:32:17.720
Who is going to Mars?
-The government.


00:32:17.880 --> 00:32:20.760
They won't let us normaI people go.


00:32:21.050 --> 00:32:23.090
Normal people.


00:32:24.760 --> 00:32:26.550
Hello, Harry.


00:32:27.460 --> 00:32:29.420
I've been very worried about you.


00:32:29.800 --> 00:32:31.630
No! Don't let him near me.


00:32:32.140 --> 00:32:34.140
Special Agent Faraday.


00:32:34.510 --> 00:32:36.590
Harry used to be a helI of a scientist.


00:32:36.760 --> 00:32:38.380
Did lots of classified stuff.


00:32:38.550 --> 00:32:42.180
We can't leave him in a regular institution
because of what he might spilI.


00:32:42.340 --> 00:32:44.090
You're referring to the Mars mission?


00:32:45.090 --> 00:32:47.930
The what?
-He told me about a mission to Mars.


00:32:50.050 --> 00:32:53.720
He's even farther gone than I thought.
If that's possible.


00:32:54.010 --> 00:32:56.720
Now, come on, Harry.
-No, please don't let him take me.


00:32:56.880 --> 00:32:58.840
Please, please.


00:33:03.800 --> 00:33:08.630
Mr. Faraday, if there's anything else
I can do for you, please let me know.


00:33:09.380 --> 00:33:10.800
Sure.


00:33:12.670 --> 00:33:14.840
<i>We've been able to contact Mars.
Life on Mars.</i>


00:33:15.010 --> 00:33:17.180
<i>We're going to Mars.</i>


00:33:18.550 --> 00:33:20.630
See you around, Jones.


00:33:23.260 --> 00:33:25.300
<i>It's all true.</i>


00:33:26.340 --> 00:33:28.140
<i>Wilson's vigilante activities...</i>


00:33:28.300 --> 00:33:31.670
<i>...kept the local white supremacists
at bay for years...</i>


00:33:31.840 --> 00:33:35.800
<i>...but his luck ran out yesterday
when he was caught by a mob and killed.</i>


00:33:36.180 --> 00:33:38.380
<i>Police say they have no suspects.</i>


00:33:38.720 --> 00:33:40.260
<i>In other news- Hey.</i>


00:33:40.420 --> 00:33:43.550
<i>Sorry to interrupt. There's something
I have to get off my chest.</i>


00:33:43.720 --> 00:33:45.720
<i>I've always used my power
to help people...</i>


00:33:45.880 --> 00:33:48.840
<i>...but the government's on my tail,
hunting me like a criminal.</i>


00:33:49.010 --> 00:33:51.010
<i>You just saw what happened
to John Wilson.</i>


00:33:51.180 --> 00:33:52.880
<i>America needs more people like him.</i>


00:33:53.140 --> 00:33:56.720
<i>But where are they going to come from
if our government keeps acting this way?</i>


00:33:57.050 --> 00:34:01.140
<i>As for me, I'm quitting, giving it up.</i>


00:34:01.300 --> 00:34:05.220
<i>Breaks my heart but there are people I love.
I don't want anything to happen to them.</i>


00:34:05.380 --> 00:34:09.460
<i>So good night, everybody, and good luck.</i>


00:34:12.380 --> 00:34:15.220
Who needed him anyway?
-Probably some kind of crook.


00:34:15.380 --> 00:34:17.720
Definitely a freak.
-Definitely.


00:34:17.880 --> 00:34:21.760
And what was with that red costume?
Red's for commies.


00:34:22.420 --> 00:34:25.340
Hey, where are you going?
-Home.


00:34:57.720 --> 00:34:59.460
Mr. Jones...


00:34:59.760 --> 00:35:01.090
...how did you locate me?


00:35:01.300 --> 00:35:05.550
I may not be the world's greatest
detective, but I have my methods.


00:35:05.930 --> 00:35:08.460
This is alI the information
I've been able to collect.


00:35:08.630 --> 00:35:09.760
It's the last of it.


00:35:11.510 --> 00:35:15.380
I thought I could make a life for myself
here among you humans.


00:35:15.550 --> 00:35:17.760
I didn't think I had a choice.


00:35:17.930 --> 00:35:19.260
But there is one now.


00:35:20.670 --> 00:35:24.300
There's just too much hatred here,
too much ignorance...


00:35:24.460 --> 00:35:27.260
...too much mindless conformity.


00:35:27.760 --> 00:35:29.300
I'm leaving.


00:35:30.460 --> 00:35:31.630
Have a nice trip.


00:35:31.800 --> 00:35:33.720
Some of us don't have that luxury.


00:35:42.550 --> 00:35:44.380
Flying Cloud, status report.


00:35:44.550 --> 00:35:46.840
Flying Cloud is go. Secure for launch.


00:35:47.010 --> 00:35:48.260
Jordan?
-Go.


00:35:48.590 --> 00:35:51.760
<i>Good luck, Flying Cloud.
God be with you.</i>


00:36:19.970 --> 00:36:21.670
Go for launch on alI points.


00:36:22.140 --> 00:36:24.140
<i>Roger, we are go for launch.</i>


00:36:34.550 --> 00:36:35.880
Ignition sequence start.


00:36:37.300 --> 00:36:39.930
<i>Primary engines engaged.</i>


00:36:40.880 --> 00:36:42.510
<i>All engines running.</i>


00:36:46.840 --> 00:36:48.880
Don't move, Martian.


00:36:51.930 --> 00:36:55.970
<i>Ten, nine, eight, seven...</i>


00:36:56.140 --> 00:36:57.840
<i>...six, five...</i>


00:36:58.260 --> 00:37:01.880
<i>...four, three, two, one.</i>


00:37:50.300 --> 00:37:52.090
Almost there.


00:38:03.880 --> 00:38:05.090
We're losing pressure.


00:38:10.460 --> 00:38:13.260
We're gonna have to take her back.
-Too risky.


00:38:13.510 --> 00:38:14.550
Jordan, listen to me.


00:38:14.720 --> 00:38:17.140
We have weapons on board.
-What?


00:38:17.300 --> 00:38:19.460
In case the Martians
turned out to be hostile.


00:38:20.140 --> 00:38:23.930
Nerve gas, germ bombs, even nuclear.


00:38:25.010 --> 00:38:27.970
Doesn't make a difference.
I can stilI land this thing.


00:38:29.590 --> 00:38:31.510
What's that?
-It's a destruct switch.


00:38:31.970 --> 00:38:34.590
I'm sorry, Jordan,
but you knew the risks.


00:38:37.930 --> 00:38:39.010
You just relax, colonel.


00:38:39.180 --> 00:38:41.180
I'll have you on the ground in no time.


00:38:41.550 --> 00:38:43.670
<i>What's going on there?
Come in, Flying Cloud.</i>


00:38:43.840 --> 00:38:46.510
<i>We've had an engine failure.
I'm gonna glide her back.</i>


00:38:46.670 --> 00:38:48.090
Negative, it's too dangerous.


00:38:48.260 --> 00:38:50.720
<i>Where's Flagg?
-Don't worry about him...</i>


00:38:50.880 --> 00:38:53.510
<i>...or your weapons. They'll both be okay.</i>


00:38:53.670 --> 00:38:55.340
Weapons?


00:38:56.420 --> 00:38:58.970
You son of a bitch.


00:38:59.760 --> 00:39:01.260
Jordan, put Flagg back on.


00:39:01.550 --> 00:39:04.420
No can do, Faraday. He's indisposed.


00:39:06.670 --> 00:39:08.090
Call in the big guy.


00:39:24.380 --> 00:39:26.010
Flagg, don't. I can land it.


00:39:26.180 --> 00:39:28.800
I can't bet the world on that, Jordan.


00:41:51.260 --> 00:41:52.300
Nuclear weapons?


00:41:52.460 --> 00:41:54.260
Nerve gas? What were you thinking?


00:41:54.590 --> 00:41:57.180
We didn't know. We're still not sure.


00:41:57.340 --> 00:41:58.460
Of what, exactly?


00:41:59.050 --> 00:42:00.840
If we can trust him.


00:42:01.010 --> 00:42:03.630
You trust me and I'm an alien.
-Yeah, but...


00:42:03.800 --> 00:42:06.550
It's because he looks
so different, isn't it?


00:42:06.930 --> 00:42:09.720
You have to admit-
-Listen, you've seen the power he has.


00:42:09.880 --> 00:42:11.930
He could leave this place
any time he wants.


00:42:12.090 --> 00:42:13.630
But he hasn't.


00:42:13.800 --> 00:42:16.220
That should telI you something.


00:42:23.220 --> 00:42:25.800
Tell me about this America, Diana.


00:42:26.050 --> 00:42:27.720
It's changed since the war.


00:42:27.880 --> 00:42:31.010
Back then, we were in the right.
It was simple.


00:42:33.220 --> 00:42:36.220
They still say they're in the right
but they don't act that way.


00:42:36.460 --> 00:42:37.720
Men.


00:42:43.010 --> 00:42:44.880
Things have changed here too, Diana.


00:42:45.050 --> 00:42:48.760
A lot of us are beginning to think we need
a leader who sticks closer to home.


00:42:49.140 --> 00:42:51.050
And who would such a leader be?


00:42:51.220 --> 00:42:52.760
You?


00:43:00.090 --> 00:43:02.800
You might need a little more seasoning.


00:44:35.670 --> 00:44:37.260
Hal Jordan.


00:44:38.090 --> 00:44:39.630
You know me?


00:44:39.800 --> 00:44:41.260
Who are you?


00:44:41.630 --> 00:44:43.840
I am...


00:44:44.630 --> 00:44:46.300
...Abin Sur.


00:44:46.550 --> 00:44:49.050
You need a doctor. Let me-


00:44:49.550 --> 00:44:51.550
Listen to me.


00:44:51.720 --> 00:44:56.220
What I have to telI you
will seem unbelievable but-


00:44:59.220 --> 00:45:04.010
I am the Green Lantern of Sector 2814.


00:45:04.180 --> 00:45:06.800
I was on my way here to help.


00:45:07.050 --> 00:45:08.880
Help? How?


00:45:09.300 --> 00:45:13.720
In the coming battle with The Centre.


00:45:13.880 --> 00:45:15.220
Center of what?


00:45:15.510 --> 00:45:20.880
It is a monstrous creature
that fears you humans so much...


00:45:21.420 --> 00:45:26.550
...it intends to eradicate every
living souI on the planet.


00:45:27.720 --> 00:45:31.050
When I was entering your atmosphere
a few days ago...


00:45:31.220 --> 00:45:34.220
...there was a huge explosion.


00:45:34.590 --> 00:45:37.800
There was too much yellow energy
for me.


00:45:37.970 --> 00:45:41.010
I ordered my ring to find you.


00:45:41.180 --> 00:45:44.260
I had to find a deserving one.


00:45:44.420 --> 00:45:47.340
A man entirely without fear.


00:45:48.590 --> 00:45:53.420
A lot of people think I'm a coward
because of what happened in the war.


00:45:53.590 --> 00:45:55.180
Did your ring telI you about that?


00:45:55.460 --> 00:45:58.420
You are no coward, Hal Jordan.


00:45:58.670 --> 00:46:01.760
To you, all life is precious.


00:46:01.930 --> 00:46:07.050
And this ring is far too powerful
to fall into the hands of someone...


00:46:07.220 --> 00:46:09.300
...who doesn't understand that.


00:46:27.590 --> 00:46:28.930
How does this thing work?


00:46:29.180 --> 00:46:31.880
The Guardians...


00:46:32.050 --> 00:46:35.630
They will...


00:46:50.420 --> 00:46:52.140
Wow, you really do know him.


00:46:52.720 --> 00:46:53.800
And you must be Robin.


00:46:54.180 --> 00:46:56.010
I hear you're quite a detective.


00:46:56.380 --> 00:46:58.460
WelI, I try not to brag, but-


00:46:58.630 --> 00:47:00.300
Have you finished your homework yet?


00:47:00.460 --> 00:47:02.970
Uh... Right.


00:47:05.970 --> 00:47:09.090
Hm. New look, a sidekick.


00:47:09.260 --> 00:47:12.010
Do you mind if I ask-?
-As a matter of fact, I do.


00:47:12.340 --> 00:47:15.840
Let's just say I set out to scare criminals,
not children.


00:47:16.220 --> 00:47:17.670
Fair enough.


00:47:18.050 --> 00:47:22.180
This alI lines up with dozens of stories
we've run in the Planet this year.


00:47:22.630 --> 00:47:25.630
The children's book
is particularly ominous.


00:47:25.800 --> 00:47:28.460
As if someone, something else...


00:47:28.630 --> 00:47:30.340
...were speaking through the author.


00:47:30.510 --> 00:47:33.930
<i>-in its wake. We have a live report
coming in from Cape Canaveral.</i>


00:47:34.090 --> 00:47:37.550
<i>The creature is hovering over
the large fuel tanks here at the Cape...</i>


00:47:37.720 --> 00:47:40.800
<i>...making it impossible for the Army
to use their missiles on it.</i>


00:47:40.970 --> 00:47:43.550
<i>Lois.
-Its wingspan is easily the length...</i>


00:47:43.720 --> 00:47:44.880
<i>...of a football field...</i>


00:47:45.050 --> 00:47:47.840
<i>...and it looks a lot like
a prehistoric pterodactyl.</i>


00:47:48.010 --> 00:47:49.970
<i>But much, much bigger.</i>


00:47:56.340 --> 00:47:59.180
I'm not sure of what it's trying to do.


00:48:41.630 --> 00:48:43.380
Diana.


00:48:44.630 --> 00:48:47.670
Haven't flown this thing in years.


00:48:48.090 --> 00:48:49.630
Guess I'm a little rusty.


00:48:49.800 --> 00:48:51.220
Easy, easy.


00:48:51.670 --> 00:48:55.800
We fought it, hard as we could, but-


00:48:58.930 --> 00:49:00.880
It's coming, KaI.


00:49:01.050 --> 00:49:03.420
It's coming here.


00:49:08.300 --> 00:49:09.300
Medic!


00:49:10.180 --> 00:49:12.970
We know this place could
never hold someone with your powers.


00:49:13.380 --> 00:49:16.800
Why do you stay?
-I'm determined to beat you at this game.


00:49:16.970 --> 00:49:19.630
Without reading your mind.


00:49:19.970 --> 00:49:22.090
Come on, level with me.


00:49:22.760 --> 00:49:24.510
Very well.


00:49:24.670 --> 00:49:28.760
I have looked into your mind,
and by extension, your heart.


00:49:28.930 --> 00:49:31.630
You honestly believe
that there wilI be a better day...


00:49:31.800 --> 00:49:33.630
...when all of this won't be necessary.


00:49:34.220 --> 00:49:39.510
To find that within you, Mr. Faraday,
has filled my heart with hope.


00:49:41.880 --> 00:49:45.140
And I have no place else to go.


00:49:48.010 --> 00:49:51.550
This just came in from Washington,
urgent.


00:49:52.670 --> 00:49:54.340
It's The Centre, isn't it?


00:49:54.510 --> 00:49:57.300
I can feeI its presence very strongly now.


00:49:58.220 --> 00:49:59.970
You're looking for a place to go?


00:50:00.260 --> 00:50:02.340
I got one helI of a destination for you.


00:50:02.510 --> 00:50:03.800
But we might not come back.


00:50:04.720 --> 00:50:05.760
I'm ready.


00:50:07.720 --> 00:50:10.300
The last time I appeared
without warning in this form...


00:50:10.460 --> 00:50:11.760
...someone died of fright.


00:50:12.010 --> 00:50:14.840
Perhaps I should take a friendlier
appearance.


00:50:15.010 --> 00:50:16.840
Suit yourself.


00:50:19.670 --> 00:50:21.380
WelI?


00:50:22.380 --> 00:50:25.970
It's okay. But real men wear pants.


00:50:35.050 --> 00:50:38.300
<i>-this absolutely unprecedented
situation off the coast of Florida.</i>


00:50:38.460 --> 00:50:40.840
<i>The combined might
of the U.S. Armed Forces...</i>


00:50:41.010 --> 00:50:43.260
<i>...had no effect on this-
-Bourbon, please.</i>


00:50:43.420 --> 00:50:45.180
<i>I hardly know what to call it.</i>


00:50:45.340 --> 00:50:48.720
<i>It appears we've reestablished contact
with our reporter at the scene.</i>


00:50:48.880 --> 00:50:53.800
<i>The only word I can find
to describe the scale of this is "biblical. "</i>


00:50:53.970 --> 00:50:58.590
<i>It's a living island,
at least 25 miles across.</i>


00:51:00.720 --> 00:51:05.180
<i>It has large ports which
discharge intense blasts of energy...</i>


00:51:05.340 --> 00:51:09.420
<i>...but which can also draw things
into the creature.</i>


00:51:10.510 --> 00:51:15.760
<i>Not two minutes ago, we watched it inhale
an entire aircraft carrier.</i>


00:51:19.050 --> 00:51:22.970
<i>The loss of life out here
is incalculable and-</i>


00:51:23.140 --> 00:51:27.550
<i>Wait. We're turning around.
We've been ordered back.</i>


00:51:27.760 --> 00:51:29.260
I have to tell you something.


00:51:29.420 --> 00:51:31.510
I'm the F...
-I already know.


00:51:31.760 --> 00:51:33.420
You what?


00:51:35.590 --> 00:51:37.260
I'm a reporter, remember?


00:51:37.420 --> 00:51:40.670
I always suspected, and I heard your voice
on the news the other night.


00:51:40.840 --> 00:51:45.090
I was only trying to protect you.
They think I'm some kind of criminal.


00:51:45.340 --> 00:51:46.760
But we know better, don't we?


00:51:49.840 --> 00:51:51.260
So, what are you waiting for?


00:51:51.420 --> 00:51:55.180
You know who's going to be there?
Superman, Wonder Woman, people like that.


00:51:55.340 --> 00:51:58.510
I'm just a guy who runs
after jewelry thieves and talking gorillas.


00:51:58.670 --> 00:52:00.010
You're more than that.


00:52:00.180 --> 00:52:02.340
And you're going to prove it.


00:52:19.880 --> 00:52:21.300
What are you doing?


00:52:23.050 --> 00:52:26.050
Where have you been?
And what happened to the simulator?


00:52:26.220 --> 00:52:27.340
Long story.


00:52:27.510 --> 00:52:30.180
Have you seen the news?
Do you have any idea what's-


00:52:32.140 --> 00:52:33.510
Oh, God.


00:52:33.670 --> 00:52:35.510
You're going down there, aren't you?


00:52:35.670 --> 00:52:38.970
Hal the pacifist is going down there
to get killed by that thing.


00:52:39.140 --> 00:52:40.550
What would you have me do?


00:52:40.720 --> 00:52:42.340
Or do you think I'm a coward too?


00:52:42.510 --> 00:52:44.510
I looked up your war record.


00:52:44.670 --> 00:52:47.010
You never fired
at those North Korean planes.


00:52:47.180 --> 00:52:50.970
Maybe I just didn't believe that what
we were doing there was worth killing for.


00:52:51.140 --> 00:52:54.510
But in that trench,
I found out what would make me kill.


00:52:54.670 --> 00:52:58.800
Survival. I would kill to survive.


00:53:02.420 --> 00:53:05.970
Aren't you going to at least say goodbye?


00:53:06.140 --> 00:53:07.800
Don't you-?


00:53:28.420 --> 00:53:30.300
Whoa. We're just here to help.


00:53:34.010 --> 00:53:37.720
We don't need help.
Especially not from you.


00:53:38.760 --> 00:53:41.550
You think you can hit me?
It's been tried before.


00:53:41.800 --> 00:53:43.720
Don't push us, mister.


00:53:52.340 --> 00:53:55.090
I see I have your attention.


00:53:55.510 --> 00:53:58.840
We face a threat big enough
to wipe us off the Earth...


00:53:59.010 --> 00:54:02.840
...and still we bicker about a mask
or a uniform.


00:54:03.010 --> 00:54:05.880
My best friend is lying upstairs right now.


00:54:06.050 --> 00:54:08.420
She would have given her life
for this country...


00:54:08.590 --> 00:54:12.380
...and I could hardly look her in the eye.
America was founded on the notion...


00:54:12.550 --> 00:54:15.340
...that a person should be free
to follow his or her destiny.


00:54:15.510 --> 00:54:18.720
But we can't do that if we're living in fear
of our own government.


00:54:19.010 --> 00:54:23.260
We need to reclaim this country
for free men and women everywhere.


00:54:23.420 --> 00:54:26.550
What about your government friends?
-That's a fair question.


00:54:27.090 --> 00:54:28.260
Superman's right.


00:54:28.420 --> 00:54:30.460
The persecution and paranoia
have to stop.


00:54:30.630 --> 00:54:34.970
From here on,
we work together as free Americans.


00:54:41.630 --> 00:54:44.720
I'm gonna fly out now
and recon this thing.


00:54:47.630 --> 00:54:50.590
When I get back,
we'Il work out a strategy.


00:54:50.760 --> 00:54:51.800
Are you with me?


00:55:53.260 --> 00:55:56.720
<i>America's champion, Superman...</i>


00:55:56.880 --> 00:56:00.720
...went down in defeat severaI hours ago.


00:56:00.880 --> 00:56:05.380
An exhaustive search
has found no sign of him.


00:56:06.300 --> 00:56:09.930
Here at the Cape,
the greatest minds in the free world...


00:56:10.090 --> 00:56:14.510
...are now working on a plan to stop
this monster...


00:56:14.670 --> 00:56:16.880
...before it reaches the coast.


00:56:17.260 --> 00:56:19.460
We cannot panic.


00:56:20.380 --> 00:56:25.180
We cannot let our sense of loss-


00:56:35.300 --> 00:56:36.550
If this book's right...


00:56:36.720 --> 00:56:39.380
...it's a whole new life form
we've never even imagined.


00:56:40.420 --> 00:56:43.930
Or it could be nothing more than
the ravings of some demented cartoonist.


00:56:46.220 --> 00:56:49.260
It's not. I assure you.


00:56:49.420 --> 00:56:52.260
And there's only one way
to stop this thing now.


00:56:52.420 --> 00:56:54.180
I want you all to listen to this man.


00:56:54.340 --> 00:56:58.260
Gentlemen, I'm Ray Palmer
from Ivy University.


00:56:58.420 --> 00:57:01.050
I've heard of you, Palmer,
and your invention.


00:57:01.220 --> 00:57:02.420
Matter reduction, right?


00:57:02.590 --> 00:57:04.930
Right. I...
-It won't work.


00:57:05.090 --> 00:57:07.340
Everything it shrinks becomes unstable.


00:57:07.510 --> 00:57:08.760
Exactly.


00:57:12.420 --> 00:57:14.340
We start with an all-out aeriaI assault.


00:57:14.510 --> 00:57:17.880
We hit the thing from every direction
at once. That's a distraction.


00:57:18.300 --> 00:57:21.050
While it's fighting the Air Corps,
we use this baby on it.


00:57:21.630 --> 00:57:24.800
This gizmo uses light to shrink things.


00:57:28.800 --> 00:57:29.930
Question...
-Wait.


00:57:30.090 --> 00:57:32.220
Everything the ray shrinks
becomes unstable.


00:57:34.800 --> 00:57:37.300
Meaning, it explodes.


00:57:37.720 --> 00:57:38.760
Still have a question?


00:57:38.930 --> 00:57:42.050
That thing out there is one
hell of a lot bigger than an orange.


00:57:42.220 --> 00:57:44.050
How are you gonna?
-It is big.


00:57:44.220 --> 00:57:47.550
And that's why we have to expose
its surface to the ray piece by piece.


00:57:47.800 --> 00:57:51.340
All in the blink of an eye?
That's impossible without Superman.


00:57:51.510 --> 00:57:55.550
No, it's not impossible, is it?


00:57:57.050 --> 00:57:58.140
Piece of cake.


00:57:58.550 --> 00:57:59.800
Any other questions?


00:57:59.970 --> 00:58:01.510
Just one.
-Jordan.


00:58:01.670 --> 00:58:04.220
About time.
-Attacking the surface won't be enough...


00:58:04.380 --> 00:58:05.670
...to distract this thing.


00:58:05.840 --> 00:58:08.720
You need someone
to go inside with bombs.


00:58:08.880 --> 00:58:10.760
You volunteering?
-He'd better...


00:58:10.930 --> 00:58:13.140
...because I'm not going in there alone.


00:58:13.300 --> 00:58:15.300
Outstanding.


00:58:24.550 --> 00:58:26.510
<i>All of you, remember...</i>


00:58:26.670 --> 00:58:29.340
<i>...today there are no Democrats,
no Republicans.</i>


00:58:29.510 --> 00:58:31.840
<i>No hawks, no doves.</i>


00:58:32.010 --> 00:58:34.880
<i>Just the naked simplicity of an absolute:</i>


00:58:35.090 --> 00:58:37.300
<i>Mankind's survival.</i>


00:58:37.840 --> 00:58:39.880
<i>Good luck to us all.</i>


00:59:11.340 --> 00:59:12.550
All right, men.


00:59:12.720 --> 00:59:16.180
Our job is to protect Flash until Morgan
and Jordan light it up.


00:59:16.340 --> 00:59:17.720
I want...
-Hey, look out!


01:01:03.670 --> 01:01:06.220
Hawk! Ah!


01:01:35.010 --> 01:01:40.380
Are you all right?
-It's attacking my mind.


01:02:32.760 --> 01:02:34.930
All of you, fight on!


01:02:35.090 --> 01:02:37.840
To the last breath, fight on!


01:02:39.010 --> 01:02:40.590
All weapons systems hot.


01:02:40.760 --> 01:02:43.880
<i>Like they say, it ain't when you go,
it's how you go.</i>


01:03:17.800 --> 01:03:20.220
Uh, Hal?
What's wrong?


01:03:20.380 --> 01:03:22.010
Whatever you see, ignore it.


01:03:22.180 --> 01:03:24.260
Just keep going. Acknowledge.


01:03:26.380 --> 01:03:28.630
Just keep going. No problem.


01:03:37.670 --> 01:03:39.180
What now?


01:03:42.340 --> 01:03:45.670
This stuff is no hallucination,
-I'll tell you that.


01:03:51.420 --> 01:03:54.010
And whatever it is,
I think it's trying to get inside.


01:03:57.760 --> 01:04:00.180
Drop the bombs,
then we'll burn our way out.


01:04:00.340 --> 01:04:01.460
Roger that.


01:04:08.090 --> 01:04:09.340
My rockets are dead.


01:04:09.510 --> 01:04:10.840
Can't open bomb bay doors.


01:04:11.010 --> 01:04:12.510
<i>Hal?
-I'm here.</i>


01:04:12.670 --> 01:04:15.510
We've had our ride
and it's time to punch our ticket.


01:04:15.670 --> 01:04:17.670
<i>Initiate manual detonation.</i>


01:04:17.840 --> 01:04:19.720
Roger.


01:04:28.800 --> 01:04:31.590
<i>Hal Jordan, you are the key.</i>


01:04:31.760 --> 01:04:33.970
<i>Your will drives the ring.</i>


01:04:34.140 --> 01:04:38.800
<i>Clear your mind
and focus on what matters.</i>


01:05:26.260 --> 01:05:28.220
Hal? What-?


01:05:28.380 --> 01:05:29.880
Later.


01:05:33.420 --> 01:05:34.760
You're afraid.


01:05:34.930 --> 01:05:36.590
It's all on me.


01:05:36.800 --> 01:05:38.140
The whole thing.


01:05:38.550 --> 01:05:40.510
We'll be there for you.


01:05:40.670 --> 01:05:42.630
We all will.


01:05:49.420 --> 01:05:50.630
Godspeed.


01:06:38.880 --> 01:06:41.590
He did it. Son of a bitch.


01:06:52.760 --> 01:06:54.010
I was afraid...


01:06:54.180 --> 01:06:56.840
...I'd be late for the victory party.


01:07:02.050 --> 01:07:03.220
Spoke too soon.


01:07:14.380 --> 01:07:18.590
That thing's gonna do a lot of damage.
Guess it's time to see what this ring can do.


01:07:18.760 --> 01:07:19.800
Hey.


01:07:23.010 --> 01:07:24.460
Sorry.


01:07:33.930 --> 01:07:36.380
That guy with the ring,
he wasn't part of the plan.


01:07:36.550 --> 01:07:37.840
Or wasn't I listening?


01:07:41.840 --> 01:07:44.380
<i>You won't be able to do it.</i>


01:07:44.550 --> 01:07:47.720
<i>It is The Centre that holds, not you.</i>


01:07:48.050 --> 01:07:50.930
I can. I can.


01:07:51.220 --> 01:07:54.760
<i>You do not have the will.</i>


01:07:55.090 --> 01:07:56.260
No?


01:07:56.420 --> 01:07:58.090
Watch.


01:08:39.260 --> 01:08:41.630
Whoo-hoo!


01:08:51.970 --> 01:08:54.140
Hey, Ace, what happened
to that buddy of yours?


01:08:54.300 --> 01:08:55.420
Hal Jordan?


01:08:55.590 --> 01:08:58.970
If I know him, he's up there somewhere
tear-assing around.


01:09:32.590 --> 01:09:34.760
I am Arthur of Atlantis.


01:09:34.930 --> 01:09:38.840
This one has been asking
for a woman named Lois.


01:10:05.220 --> 01:10:08.880
<i>The pioneers gave up their safety,
their comfort...</i>


01:10:09.050 --> 01:10:13.420
<i>...and sometimes their lives
to build our new West.</i>


01:10:13.590 --> 01:10:18.180
<i>They were determined
to make the new world strong and free...</i>


01:10:18.340 --> 01:10:21.180
<i>...an example to the world.</i>


01:10:21.420 --> 01:10:25.090
<i>Some would say that those struggles
are all over.</i>


01:10:25.260 --> 01:10:27.880
<i>That all the horizons have been explored.</i>


01:10:28.050 --> 01:10:30.420
<i>That all the battles have been won.</i>


01:10:30.590 --> 01:10:34.140
<i>That there is no longer
an American frontier.</i>


01:10:36.090 --> 01:10:40.420
<i>And we stand today on the edge
of a new frontier.</i>


01:10:40.590 --> 01:10:45.010
<i>The frontier of unknown opportunities
and perils.</i>


01:10:45.180 --> 01:10:51.010
<i>Beyond that frontier are uncharted areas
of science and space.</i>


01:10:51.180 --> 01:10:54.010
<i>Unsolved problems of peace and war.</i>


01:10:54.180 --> 01:10:58.930
<i>Unconquered pockets
of ignorance and prejudice.</i>


01:11:00.260 --> 01:11:02.300
<i>I'm asking each of you...</i>


01:11:02.460 --> 01:11:05.930
<i>...to be pioneers
towards that new frontier.</i>


01:11:06.090 --> 01:11:10.510
<i>My call is to the young at heart,
regardless of age.</i>


01:11:10.670 --> 01:11:13.260
<i>Can we carry through in an age...</i>


01:11:13.420 --> 01:11:17.880
<i>...where we will witness not only new
breakthroughs in weapons of destruction...</i>


01:11:18.050 --> 01:11:21.380
<i>...but also a race for mastery
of the sky and the rain...</i>


01:11:21.550 --> 01:11:25.300
<i>...the ocean and the tides,
the far side of space...</i>


01:11:25.460 --> 01:11:28.300
<i>...and the inside of men's minds?</i>


01:11:29.180 --> 01:11:32.140
<i>All mankind waits upon our decision.</i>


01:11:32.300 --> 01:11:36.970
<i>A whole world looks to see
what we shall do.</i>


01:11:37.460 --> 01:11:42.970
<i>And we cannot fail their trust.
And we cannot fail to try.</i>
